From 072ff2b67a80264f4db28503172b932634c4b353 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:38:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] update pause: passive rows wait while a turn is
 parked; a drain-fenced automation head settles

On laptop-1 on 2026-11-13 (agent.log through agent.log.3, re-counted 14:31 PST), a core update
parked 15 gateway turns. 9 resumed ("auto-continue scheduled"). 6 automation turns (Kanban notice
batches) were dropped ("Lost automation admission ... settled interrupted (not replayed)", at 09:59
twice, 10:25, 10:38 and 13:58 twice). The discriminator: each dropped turn's chat got a
"notice row written" between the park and the resume, and no resumed turn's chat did. In one chat (20261026_235722_bef6c6) the drain then paused the
FIFO, and every turn was refused for 1 h 45 min until the next gateway boot.

Five whys
1. The parked turn's checkpoint was invalid on resume: its receipt was gone and the admission ended
   terminal/interrupted (seq 5234).
2. A passive Kanban notice row (914739, 12:13:06) was appended after the checkpointed tool suffix
   (914622..914700). _binding requires the transcript tail to be that suffix, so the proof failed.
3. Passive writers only defer on a live turn lease (SessionTurnLeaseLostError), and a parked turn
   holds no lease. Nothing checked for a pending update checkpoint.
4. (stall branch) The drain's invalid_checkpoint path called refuse_checkpoint and then _pause, and
   never ran the GW-10 settle. An unattended head was settled only at boot or on a later claim, so
   the paused queue waited for the next owner restart. _pause logged nothing.
Root: the checkpoint ("nothing written after the suffix") and the passive-row writers ("append when
no live lease") disagreed. Separately, the drain's fence path skipped GW-10.

Fix
- hermes_state_update_pause.parked_update_turn / refuse_parked_write: a started admission with a
  gateway.update_checkpoint.v1.<id> receipt fences its logical target, the receipt's physical tip
  and its physical chain. This is checked inside the writer transaction.
- SessionDB._check_transcript_write_guards: every lease-less caller that opts in through
  reject_active_turn_lease (passive writers and user mutations) now gets the same retryable
  SessionTurnLeaseLostError ("busy") while the conversation's turn is parked. Callers already
  rewind and retry on that error, so the notice rides the resumed turn or the next pass. Paths
  covered: append_kanban_notice/record_kanban_notice (kanban_unloaded, kanban_remote_notices,
  session_notifications, reap_notices), append_completion_note, append_delegation_delivery,
  producer_admission.commit_delivery, prompt_admission.admit_prompt/mark_dispatch_failed,
  replace_messages(reject_active_turn_lease), legacy refusal repair, and mutation guards. The lease
  holder's own writes are not fenced.
- SessionAuthority drain: after refuse_checkpoint fences a head, settle_unattended_unknown settles
  it if it is unattended, and the drain continues to the queued follower. A turn a person sent still
  pauses.
- SessionAuthority._pause logs every pause: WARNING, or INFO for the transient session_busy and
  runtime_draining reasons, which would otherwise log on every worker wait.

Not fenced here (unguarded append_message writers, no lease check either): gateway/mirror.py
(send_message mirror), the TUI model_switch marker, the Stop notice, the shutdown spool replay and
the TUI submit row. These are follow-up material.

Proof
- RED on f4694c980f with only the tests applied: 19 failed. Passive-write store tests: DID NOT
  RAISE. Drain fence test: the follower never ran (pause). Pause-logging tests: no log line.
- GREEN: tests/hermes_state/test_parked_turn_passive_writes.py (15) and
  tests/gateway/test_parked_automation_fence_settles.py (7) pass, plus 256 affected test files
  (update pause, GW-10, Kanban notice and passive writer suites).
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok (FILE_LINES on hermes_state_messages.py offset).

Kanban: t_01a1d6f94ac774a2
